## S3F Phase 2: Domain Spoofing / Typosquatting Detection
##
## Description: Detects emails from domains similar to your organization's domain
## S3F Phase: 2 (Pretexting & Deception)
## S3F Technique: 2.1 (Impersonation)
## MITRE ATT&CK: T1566.001 (Phishing: Spear Phishing Attachment)
## Severity: High
##
## Prerequisites:
## - Email gateway logs ingested to Splunk
## - Index: email (adjust as needed)
## - Fields: sender_domain, recipient, subject, sender_email
##
## False Positives:
## - Legitimate partner domains with similar names
## - Sister companies or subsidiaries
## - Acquired companies
##
## Tuning:
## 1. Replace "yourcompany.com" with your actual domain
## 2. Add known partner domains to whitelist
## 3. Adjust Levenshtein distance threshold (currently 2)
## 4. Consider adding reputation scoring

index=email sourcetype=email_gateway
| rex field=sender_email "(?<sender_domain>[^@]+)$"
| eval org_domain="yourcompany.com"
| eval distance=levenshtein(sender_domain, org_domain)
| where distance <= 2 AND sender_domain != org_domain
| search NOT [| inputlookup whitelist_domains.csv | fields domain | rename domain as sender_domain]
| eval risk_score = case(
    distance == 1, 90,
    distance == 2, 70,
    1==1, 50
  )
| eval s3f_phase="2.1"
| eval s3f_technique="Impersonation"
| eval severity="high"
| eval mitre_attack="T1566.001"
| table _time, sender_email, sender_domain, recipient, subject, distance, risk_score, s3f_phase, severity
| sort - risk_score

## Alert Configuration (Splunk Enterprise Security)
## --------------------------------------------------
## Alert Trigger: Number of Results > 0
## Throttle: 1 hour (per sender_domain)
## Alert Actions:
##   - Send email to SOC
##   - Create notable event
##   - Quarantine email (via integration)
##
## Notable Event Fields:
##   - urgency: high
##   - owner: unassigned
##   - status: new
##   - category: phishing
##
## Response Actions:
##   1. Quarantine all emails from sender_domain
##   2. Alert recipients who received the email
##   3. Check if anyone clicked links or replied
##   4. Report domain to abuse contacts / registrar
##   5. Update threat intel with malicious domain
